# Copper Linux — the target that groups Copper's own services.
#
# Why a target of our own instead of hanging everything off multi-user.target:
# the ordering requirements here are real and they are Copper's, not the
# distro's. The console must come up after the wizard can talk (the wizard
# prompts on the same tty), and after the seat exists (Hyprland opens the seat
# the moment the user types starthyprland). Expressing that as
# multi-user.target.wants/ symlinks would work but would say nothing about why
# the order is what it is, and the next person to add a unit would have to
# rediscover it.
#
# multi-user.target wants copper.target; copper.target wants the units that do
# the work. DefaultDependencies=no is not needed: this target has no ordering
# of its own beyond what it inherits, and inheriting the normal shutdown
# ordering is what makes `systemctl isolate` and a clean poweroff behave.
#
# handcrafted by 12hrformat (SYSTEMD-MIGRATION.md, phase 1)
[Unit]
Description=Copper session target (wizard, console, seat, network)
